// Release build settings for the MyApp target, wired in by project.yml's configFiles.
//
// It never includes Config/Local.xcconfig: that file holds one person's development
// team for `just run-device`, which builds Debug. The one Release device build,
// `just build-device`, compiles and links for the iOS device SDK with
// CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, so it takes no team and is never signed or installed: no
// signed Release route to a device exists. An app that adds distribution revisits this.

// The production API, read by Core's AppConfiguration under the APIBaseURL key. The
// `.invalid` host is a placeholder that never resolves (RFC 6761) until the app names
// its own server; `/$()/` keeps the `//` that an xcconfig would read as a comment.
// Never a secret here — this file is committed and the value ships in Info.plist.
API_BASE_URL = https:/$()/api.invalid/v1
